content.text:
Both tabs are now fully functional with stronger end-to-end behavior.

## What I Fixed

1. Added OS-aware payload type syncing for Active Exploit in [HadesAI.py](file:///c:/Users/ek930/OneDrive/Desktop/X12/Hades-AI/HadesAI.py#L6099-L6180) so invalid Linux/Windows payload combinations are no longer selectable.
2. Added payload option refresh hook on OS change and initial tab load in [HadesAI.py](file:///c:/Users/ek930/OneDrive/Desktop/X12/Hades-AI/HadesAI.py#L6115-L6155).
3. Hardened payload generation flow in [HadesAI.py](file:///c:/Users/ek930/OneDrive/Desktop/X12/Hades-AI/HadesAI.py#L8766-L8785):
1. validates attacker port is numeric;
2. handles empty payload generation cleanly with user feedback.
4. Hardened fuzz flow in [HadesAI.py](file:///c:/Users/ek930/OneDrive/Desktop/X12/Hades-AI/HadesAI.py#L8786-L8819):
1. normalizes URL (`https://` auto-prefix);
2. uses attacker IP/port consistently for generated payloads;
3. gracefully handles empty payload sets;
4. handles malformed/non-dict result rows without crashes.
5. Improved exploit results rendering robustness in [HadesAI.py](file:///c:/Users/ek930/OneDrive/Desktop/X12/Hades-AI/HadesAI.py#L8804-L8815) for error and indicator display.
6. Tightened Request Injection completion reporting in [HadesAI.py](file:///c:/Users/ek930/OneDrive/Desktop/X12/Hades-AI/HadesAI.py#L8865-L8868) to include both interesting responses and error counts.

## Verification

1. `python -X utf8 -m py_compile HadesAI.py` passed.
2. Offscreen GUI smoke tests confirmed:
1. Active Exploit payload list updates by OS (`windows` no longer shows Linux-only `reverse_shell`);
2. fuzz URL auto-normalization works;
3. Request Injection runs and fills result rows reliably.

